            <ArticleTitle>Headaches.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>137-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although classification can be difficult, determining the type of headache, such as tension, migraine or cluster, aids in the formulation of a therapeutic approach. Treatment involves regulation rather than cure. Acute and prophylactic pharmacotherapy and control of stress through behavior modification, relaxation training and biofeedback are methods of management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
